# rules_rust drops the cc_toolchain's static C++ runtime
# (`static_runtime_lib`: hermetic-llvm's libc++/libc++abi/libunwind, the
# sole provider of the `_Unwind_*` symbols rust std needs since the
# toolchain links with `--unwindlib=none`) in two places this patch fixes:
# `rust_doc_test` links (every doc test fails to link with undefined
# `_Unwind_*`) and dylib/cdylib links (rules_rust links the — here empty —
# dynamic runtime instead, and since shared-library links don't fail on
# undefined symbols the breakage only surfaces at runtime: dlopen of e.g.
# libnss_icos.so fails, leaving GuestOS unable to resolve "hostos" and
# nft unable to load the orchestrator's firewall rules).
